course: dictionary
lesson: 2406
title: Customer: the person who buys
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A customer is a person who buys things in a shop, or uses a service such as a café or a hairdresser. Look for clues in the sentence: who comes in, who pays, who is served. «A boy in Colorado runs a lemonade stand, and he learns to talk to customers.» The customers are the people who buy his lemonade.
explain: A customer can also order or use a service, not just buy things. «Each customer bought a cup» means each person who came to the stand paid for one. A regular customer is someone who keeps coming back, like a friend of the shop.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Shops cover the money they lose to stealing partly by raising prices, so honest customers pay too.» Put in "people who buy things" and the sentence still makes sense: honest people who buy things pay the higher prices too.
fact: A customer is a person who buys things in a shop or uses a service.
fact: «A regular customer» is someone who keeps coming back.
fact: «Customer service» is how a shop or company looks after the people who use it.
fact: «The customer is always right» is a saying that shops often use.
fact: «Child prices» are an agreement between a cinema and its customers, and saying a false age breaks the deal.
exercise: «A boy in Colorado runs a lemonade stand, and he learns to talk to customers.» Who are the customers in this sentence? | *The people who buy his lemonade | The people who wash the cups | The cups and the price tags | The boy's dad
exercise: Find and copy the word for a person who buys things in a shop. | *customer | lemonade | stand | price
exercise: «A regular customer» means what? | *Someone who keeps coming back | A cup of lemonade | A worker who sells the goods | Someone who never buys anything
test: «Each customer bought a cup.» What does this tell you? | The shop was closed all day | The cups were free | *Each person who came paid for a cup | Nobody bought anything
test: What is customer service? | A worker who counts change | A list of prices on a wall | *How a shop looks after the people who use it | A type of cash register
exam: Which word means a person who buys things in a shop or uses a service? | *customer | cloud | teacher | ladder
